  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-03-15T21:47:54.407Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "# Gimbal mode / Mavic mode / Cinematic mode\n\n- Being able to **control camera angle separately** while the drone is still kinda floaty or flying in a set direction, is a big part of doing cinematic drone shots. Same with zoom\n\n- Moreso, using gamepad triggers for changing gimbal angle is *already ergonomically good* - triggers are analogue, which allows for slow, smooth, yet variable angle change\n\n- Also, this style of flying is more beginner-friendly and gamepad-friendly than FPV, which would make drone mode a more desirable feature for many people outside of FPV-community (which means **💰VRC+ cash💰** )\n\n- And, i bet this mode would make a LOT of VRChat content!\n\n# Disabling Z-axis while auto-leveling\n\n- Making it possible to compensate only yaw and roll, would allow for some really cool shots with altitude change\n\n- (bug?) Whenever i do a slow height change in auto-leveled mode and zero my stick (stop sending inputs to change throttle), drone gets yanked in the opposite direction. Not sure if a bug or misconfiguration on my side\n\n# FPV-drone mode suggestions\n\n- Being able to **make own drone pickuppable** by either friends or anybody, would allow some cute interactions between a drone operator and their viewers\n\n- Inclusion of FPV drones with decent physics already provokes drone-based events (racing, freestyle aerobatics), and being able to **differentiate between different players drones** without looking at nametags is crucial, and can be done with a **color change**, and/or, a **drone model change**.\n\n- I can see being able to **turn off the trail** as a desirable feature for immersion. Probably simple to implement, too!\n\n- **Sharing own drone feed**, if technically possible, would allow to host racing events without an external player\n\n- Racing feature - **hitbox tilt**. Usually racing drones are starting while tilted, not vertical. Making it able to tilt drone's hitbox is the simplest way to do it.\n\n# Quality of life changes for FPV operators\n\n- **Horizon level** is a widely used feature IRL\n\n- **Switch Auto-Leveling** by a keybind / gamepad button.",
